Package: ghostfs
Version: 0.3.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: HackerOS Project <packaging@hackeros.local>
Depends: libfuse3-3 (>= 3.10), calamares (>= 3.2), python3, initramfs-tools | dracut
Recommends: tpm2-tools
Conflicts: ghostfs-nocalamares
Description: GhostFS filesystem + Calamares default-installer integration
 GhostFS is a cybersecurity-oriented FUSE filesystem (MAC labels, forensics
 chain-of-custody logging, IDS, canary files, mandatory-by-default
 encryption in cybersec builds).
 .
 This package installs BOTH:
   1. The ghostfs / ghostfs-cybersec binaries, admin tooling, and
      initramfs early-boot mount hooks.
   2. Calamares job modules (ghostfs-mkfs / ghostfs-mount / ghostfs-umount)
      AND a patch applied to the already-installed Calamares configuration
      (/etc/calamares/modules/partition.conf and /etc/calamares/settings.conf)
      that makes GhostFS the ONLY filesystem the installer offers — no
      ext4, no btrfs, no xfs. Installing this package turns any
      Calamares-based installer image into a GhostFS-only installer.
 .
 This package assumes Calamares is ALREADY installed on the system (see
 Depends). It does not install or configure Calamares itself beyond the
 targeted config patch described above, and it reverts that patch cleanly
 on removal (see DEBIAN/postrm).
